  "prompt": "For each channel, what share of net revenue came from orders worth more than 1,000 EUR? Use the sales table; an order's value is the sum of its lines' net_revenue_eur, and an order counts as big when its value is above 1000. Return two columns, in this order: channel and big_order_share, the net revenue of the channel's big orders divided by all of the channel's net revenue, as a fraction from 0 to 1. Return one row for each channel. Do not round. Any row order is fine.",
